  "what_this_test_is": "PRIMARY (b): direct subspace check \u2014 per-position tail subspace of OUR J_t (bottom 10% of its 128 \u03c3, right singular vectors, R^1024) vs tail subspace of the LENS J_22 (bottom 10% of 1024 \u03c3): overlap = \u2016V_our_tail^T V_lens_tail\u2016_F\u00b2/r_our. This is the TZ's 'symmetry with Anthropic' claim. SECONDARY (a): dual sparsity/tail correlation in both bases (rho_our vs rho_lens; the old version reported only the lens-internal rho_lens, which is NOT the TZ question). docs/E38_fixes.md part-2 \u00a71.",
  "note": "Lens fit on HINDI (finewiki@hi), docs English. Lens J_22 is a position-averaged [1024,1024] Jacobian; our J_t is per-position [128,1024]. Both act on the same h_t \u2208 R^1024 at L22 \u2014 the right-singular comparison is well-defined there. Author flags the lens 'experimental/unvalidated'; validity gate = bounded spectrum of J_22. Per TZ: do NOT substitute 9B results (different D).",
